Given the private method and no refactor possible, I will write a test that uses reflection to invoke SendMessageChunk and verify that it completes without throwing exceptions when valid data is set in the private fields. I will also verify that it does not throw when the HttpClient call is made (though we cannot mock HttpClient here).

I will write a test that sets the private fields m_botid, m_apikey, m_channelId, and m_topicId to valid values, then calls SendMessageChunk via reflection and asserts that the task completes successfully.

